\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Jesus, my hope,
\par For me offered up,
\par Who with clamour pursued Thee 
\par to Calvary's top,
\par The blood Thou hast shed,
\par For me let it plead,
\par And declare Thou hast died in Thy
\par murderer's stead.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Come then from above,
\par Its hardness remove,
\par And vanquish my heart with the
\par Sense of Thy love;
\par Thy love on the tree
\par Display unto me,
\par And the servant of sin in a moment 
\par is free.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Neither passion nor pride 
\par Thy Cross can abide,
\par But melt in the fountain that streams
\par From Thy side:
\par Let Thy life-giving blood
\par Remove all my load,
\par And purge, my foul conscience, and 
\par Bring me to God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Now, now let me know
\par Its virtues below,
\par Let it wash me, and I shall be whiter
\par Than snow;
\par Let it hallow my heart,
\par And throughout convert,
\par And make me, O Lord, in the world
\par as Thou art.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Each moment applied
\par My weakness to hide,
\par Thy blood be upon me, and always 
\par abide:
\par My Advocate prove
\par With the Father above,
\par And speak me at last to the throne 
\par of Thy love. 
\par               Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

